"quests": {
"main": {
"giver": "maud",
"have": 0,
"id": "main",
"main": true,
"reward": {},
"stage": 0,
"state": "active",
"steps": [{
"at": "cinderwick",
"t": "reach",
"text": "There is smoke to the <dir:S:cinderwick:start>. Find shelter before nightfall."
}, {
"ask": "I was cast out. I have nowhere else to go.",
"give": [["beacon_oil", 1]],
"say": "Then you are one of us. Everyone here was thrown away by somebody.

Listen. When I was a girl there were nine fires on the high places, tended by the Order, and the night did not come within sight of them. One by one they went dark. Now it comes everywhere.

There is a dead beacon on the ridge to the west. I have kept one jar of the old oil for forty years, waiting for someone foolish enough to carry it there. Take it. Pour it in the bowl, and keep the flame alive until it holds. Do not leave it, whatever comes.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Speak with the elder of Cinderwick.",
"who": "maud"
}, {
"beacon": 0,
"t": "kindle",
"text": "Kindle the Beacon of Restraint, <dir:B:0:cinderwick> of Cinderwick, and keep the flame until it holds."
}, {
"ask": "The beacon burns.",
"say": "I saw it from the wall. I wept, and I am not ashamed of it.

There is no more of the old oil. But the Lantern Well still draws lamp oil from the deep, and Benedek the oilwright knows the measure his father used for the Order. Go to the Well, <dir:S:lanternwell:cinderwick> of here. Ask him to teach you.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Return to Maud.",
"who": "maud"
}, {
"ask": "Maud sent me. I need beacon oil.",
"flag": "oilcraft",
"give": [["beacon_oil", 1]],
"say": "So the ridge fire was you. I wondered who had been fool enough.

The measure is this: two of lamp oil, ten of salt to cleanse it, four of ash-bloom to make it burn white. Render it slowly, at a proper bench, with a fire close by. Here. Take what I have made, and learn to make the rest yourself. There are eight more bowls out there, and I am too old to carry anything up a hill.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Find Benedek the oilwright at the Lantern Well.",
"who": "benedek"
}, {
"n": 4,
"t": "count",
"text": "Kindle more of the dead beacons. Render beacon oil at a workbench from lamp oil, salt and ash-bloom."
}, {
"ask": "The beacons were made to burn forever. Why did they go out?",
"say": "I asked the dead the same thing, the night your third fire was lit. They were very quiet for a long time.

Then they told me. The beacons did not fail. They were put out, by hand, one by one, by living people who walked up to them with sand and wet sacking. The dead say the hands came from Gallowmere, on the dry lake to the <dir:S:gallowmere:mourners>.

Go carefully. People who will put out a light are people who have made a bargain with the dark.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Something about the beacons is wrong. The gravekeeper of Mourner's Rest listens to the dead. Ask her.",
"who": "ione"
}, {
"ask": "You put out the beacons.",
"say": "Yes. I did. My father did. His father before him.

You think the night comes from nowhere. It comes up out of a mouth in the earth, <dir:B:8:gallowmere> of here, where the ninth beacon stood. When the ninth was lit, the mouth was quiet. Then it swallowed the beacon whole, tower and bowl and keepers, and it began to speak.

It asked for the other eight. It said: put them out, and I will leave Gallowmere standing. So we did. And we are standing. Do you understand? Every fire you light, it will want back. Light all eight, and it will have to come up and take them itself. Perhaps then you can do what we could not.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Go to Gallowmere, on the dry lake far to the <dir:S:gallowmere:cinderwick>, and speak with its warden.",
"who": "corvin"
}, {
"n": 5,
"t": "count",
"text": "Kindle a fifth beacon. Five fires, and the dark will have to turn and look at you."
}, {
"ask": "Five are burning. The sea has opened.",
"say": "And the mouth breathed. Did you feel it? Every bowl still dark has been fouled. Oil will slide off it now like water off tar.

A fouled bowl wants something from beyond the shore before it will take. The first is Deep Oil. My grandfather spoke of it: lamp oil, rendered at a bench with the ichor of the thing in the Kraken-Bell. The Bell-Wound. Bring it down and it bleeds green.

The sea took everything from us once. Now you have to go and take something back from it.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Five fires burn, and the sea has opened. Return to the warden of Gallowmere.",
"who": "corvin"
}, {
"key": "deep_oil",
"n": 6,
"t": "count",
"text": "Kindle a sixth beacon. A fouled bowl wants Deep Oil first: lamp oil and the Bell-Wound's ichor, rendered at a bench."
}, {
"ask": "The sixth bowl took the Deep Oil.",
"say": "The drowned are talking now. They have never talked before.

They were the Fleet. They sailed to Quietglass with the Order's last ships, and kept a log to the end. Its last page names the bowls, one by one, as they were fouled. They say a bowl will remember its name if you read it the page.

The log is still in Quietglass. Light the lane there first, or the deep will have you before the glass does.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Six fires. The gravekeeper of Mourner's Rest has heard the dead again.",
"who": "ione"
}, {
"key": "fleet_log",
"n": 7,
"t": "count",
"text": "Kindle a seventh beacon. A fouled bowl wants the Fleet Log, from Quietglass, reached by a lit sea lane."
}, {
"ask": "Seven fires burn across the sea.",
"say": "We saw the seventh from the Thing-field. The old men wept, and the young ones asked why.

The eighth is the hard one. The law says: what the Mouth breathes on, a great heart must warm. The far lands have five great ones, the Ice Hall's mother among them. Take the heart of any one, and carry it home to your bowl.

We will speak your name here while you are gone. We keep names.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Seven fires. Sail to Hearthholm on the Frostmark and speak with its law-speaker.",
"who": "sigrun"
}, {
"key": "heart",
"n": 8,
"t": "count",
"text": "Kindle an eighth beacon. A fouled bowl wants the heart of a far great one."
}, {
"ask": "Eight are burning. What now?",
"give": [["beacon_oil", 2]],
"say": "Now it is angry. I have not heard it this loud since I was a boy.

The ninth bowl stands at the lip of the mouth, <dir:B:8:gallowmere> of here, choked with earth and fouled besides. It wants a coal from every far shore: the Frostmark, the Sunward Reach, the Pale Steppe. Each has a shrine-bowl the Order built. Light them and carry one coal from each.

Then pour the oil. The thing below will come up to put it out. If you keep that flame, it will have to go back down, and stay down.

Take this. It is the last oil Gallowmere hid from the dark. I never had the courage to use it. Gallowmere will stand with you on the lip. That is the least we owe.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "Eight fires burn. Return to the warden of Gallowmere.",
"who": "corvin"
}, {
"beacon": 8,
"key": "coals",
"t": "kindle",
"text": "Bring a coal from the shrine-bowl of each Far Shore, then kindle the Beacon of Stillness at the lip of the mouth, and keep it while the thing below comes up to put it out."
}, {
"ask": "The ninth burns. The mouth is quiet.",
"say": "I know. The whole camp came out to look. You can see it from here, a white thread in the <dir:B:8:cinderwick>, like the one I remember.

The nights will still come. The waste is still the waste. Forms will still walk out of the dark where the fires do not reach. But they will not come for everything, and they will not come forever.

The waste is not saved, survivor. It is kept. And now there is someone to keep it.",
"t": "talk",
"text": "It is done. Return to Cinderwick.",
"who": "maud"
}],
"title": "The Dead Beacons"
}
}
},
